SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Bali 1928: A Musical Journey Back in Time at Desa Potato Head
LOCATION:Desa Potato Head
DESCRIPTION:Bali’s extraordinary and otherworldly culture was once the is
 land’s most enticing allure. Before beaches and resorts\, it was dance\,
  art\, music and ceremony that captured the imagination – a vibrant way 
 of life that intertwined nature and ritual into the everyday. The year was
  1928\, and such was this cultural fascination that German record labels O
 deon and Beka sent engineers to Bali to capture a sound quite like anythin
 g they had heard before: the rhythmic reverberations of the gamelan\, and 
 the ethereal voices of Balinese song. Around this time\, pioneering resear
 chers like the ethnomusicologist Colin McPhee\, artist and author Miguel C
 ovarrubias\, and art collector Rolf de Maré captured silent film footage 
 of ceremonies\, dancers and everyday life. For decades these lay in archiv
 es\, unseen and unheard by those depicted. Fast forward to 2013. Dr. Edwar
 d Herbst\, Arbiter of Cultural Traditions New York\, together with ITB STI
 KON Bali\, began a repatriation project\, Arsip Bali 1928 \, scoping the w
 orld for these recordings and bringing them back to Bali.\n\nMore info: ht
 tps://www.nowbali.co.id/upcoming-events/bali-1928-a-musical-journey-back-i
 n-time-at-desa-potato-head/\n\nPlease verify with the organizer before att
 ending.
URL:https://www.nowbali.co.id/upcoming-events/bali-1928-a-musical-journey-b
 ack-in-time-at-desa-potato-head/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
END:VEVENT
