LOCATION:Black Garlic
DESCRIPTION:On Friday\, 20 November 2026\, a special culinary collaboration
  will take place between Black Garlic at Adiwana Alas Harum and Dapur Bali
  Mula\, as the two culinary establishments present Rooted in Bali. A one-n
 ight dining event\, Rooted in Bali celebrates Balinese culinary and cultur
 al heritage through thoughtfully prepared dishes\, storytelling\, and the 
 performing arts\, offering guests a deeper understanding and appreciation 
 of the island’s culinary roots and the traditions that continue to shape
  its identity. When it comes to food\, there is a common thread shared uni
 versally: it tells the story of place\, its people\, and the traditions pa
 ssed down through generations. In Bali\, culinary heritage is deeply roote
 d in local ingredients\, age-old cooking methods\, and knowledge preserved
  within village communities.\n\nMore info: https://www.nowbali.co.id/upcom
 ing-events/rooted-in-bali-black-garlic-x-dapur-bali-mula/\n\nPlease verify
